    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by the elite profile of **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who draws a prime matchup against Scherzer. With a high-upside xERA of 5.10 and a slow delivery profile that enhances stolen base potential, **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary anchor for both power and our high-priority need for speed. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.93) remains a \"Strong\" play despite a neutral platoon disadvantage; the projection leans heavily on the porous 4.77 xERA of Bassitt, making him our most reliable source for RBI production. **Kyle Tucker** (68.82) also provides excellent efficiency, as his ability to consistently find high-leverage spots keeps him well above the \"Strong\" threshold.\n\nTactical platoon advantages are fueling several of our mid-tier starts. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.53) sees a significant bump to 64.53 due to a favorable dynamic platoon split against McLean, and **Jackson Merrill** (57.57) receives a similar 13% boost, confirming their roles in the bottom half of the order. **Henry Bolte** (57.59) is another high-value play; while the raw base projection was modest, a 10% boost for the hitter-friendly park conditions elevates him above the marginal tier. Conversely, **Wade Meckler** (42.38) is our most tenuous start; while he holds a platoon edge against Cavalli, the opposing starter\u2019s elite 3.24 xERA significantly dampens his ceiling, keeping him just above our \"Below Floor\" cutoff.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision today involved **Tommy White**, whose 49.41 score fell narrowly short of our primary starters. While **Tommy White** benefits from the same park factors as **Henry Bolte**, a lower spot in the batting order and the lack of a platoon advantage relegated him to the pine. We are continuing to monitor the health of **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages** on the IL, as their absence necessitates these tighter margins in our daily start/sit optimization. With no major weather concerns, the focus remains on exploiting the favorable matchups against Scherzer and Bassitt to gain ground in the 5x5 standings.",
